  "revised": "2026-10-17",
  "source": "Advantech, \"ADAM-4000 Data Acquisition Modules User's Manual\", Edition 10.7, Appendix G (I/O Modbus mapping table)",
  "sources": [{"title": "ADAM-4000 Data Acquisition Modules User's Manual", "version": "Edition 10.7", "url": "https://www.kolbinger.at/DAQM/manuals/ADAM-4000%20series%20User%20Manual.pdf", "note": "Appendix G, table 5; type codes from chapters 5 and 6"}],
  "notes": [
    "Addresses are the Modicon numbers of the manual (00001 = coil 1, 40001 = holding register 1).",
    "The module ships with the ADAM ASCII protocol; Appendix H of the manual switches it to Modbus RTU.",
    "Channel values are raw 16-bit values of the range chosen by each channel's type code; the manual gives the conversion for the ASCII protocol only."
